WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-It's good to see you buddy.
-Good to see you.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:05.601
-i haven't seen you
since "Top Gun: Maverick"

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:06.834
was the number-one --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.467
-The number-one movie that --
I think it's --

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.634
I think it's --
I think it's the fifth highest

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.200
grossing film
in American history.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.334
-Yeah.
-Congratulations, buddy.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.734
-Yeah, still climbing.
-You did it.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.067
-Every day.
-Yeah, every -- that is correct.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.567
-Yeah.
-Uh, it's bigger than

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:21.734
we even thought
it was gonna be.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.634
-Oh, for sure.
-It was fantastic.

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.734
-I know, people just --
people really love --

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.934
Well, they love Tom Cruise,
which -- as they should.

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.234
He's dedicated...
-Of course.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:30.934
-...so much of his life
to entertaining audiences.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.467
But people just love "Top Gun."

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.234
-Yeah.
-They cannot get enough of it.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.434
-I love the story, though.
I love you.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.367
You did it so -- you were --
it was just --

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.467
Everything was great.
-Thank you.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.734
-Jennifer Connelley.
-I know, right?

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.701
She's so good.
-The greatest in everything.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.234
But we had --
-Val, a nice --

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.267
a really touching performance
from Val.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.968
-I lost it.
I even knew that was

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.801
gonna happen, and I --
I watched it, and I was like --

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:52.968
I still lost it.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.133
-How did you know
it was gonna happen?

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.667
-I have an inside scoop.
-A little inside --

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:56.767
-Yeah, yeah.
-Well, you're in the biz, Jimmy.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.400
-Well, you know, I had Jon --

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.367
Jon Hamm was on the show
a couple times.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.934
And he told me that, you know,
you met the royals...

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.100
-Yes.
-...because you screened it

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.601
in London.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.934
-And it was like -- and it --
and he was telling me, he goes,

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.968
"Yeah, it was really
interesting and fun."

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.434
And he said that the cast
was all told,

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.367
"Hey, be very polite.
Don't say too much."

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:18.334
-Oh, they give -- they give you,
like, a full kind of rules,

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.801
like do's and don'ts.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:23.067
And there's, you know, a lot of
etiquette, which deservingly so.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.367
So, yeah, I was actually --
I kind of had a sheet to prep

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.434
to make sure
I didn't mess it up.

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:28.701
-But then he said --
-Yeah.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.200
-Well, I have just a photo.
And I just want you

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.934
to explain the photo,
'cause here's you talking.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.267
-Yeah.
-There's Jennifer Connelley.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.901
-Right.
-Little concerned.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.534
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.167
-Laughing.
-Sure.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.334
-Right?
Kate Middleton laughing.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:40.334
And then --
-Yeah.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.000
-He's going, "Mm-hmm."
-"Mm-hmm."

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.767
Yeah.
-And so what is happening?

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.868
Can you tell us the story of
what's going on with this?

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.367
-I think right off the bat,
I messed up.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.133
You're not supposed to, like,
extend your hand

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.734
right off the bat unless --
unless they do.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.133
But I felt the vibe,
so I was like, "I'm --"

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.901
I was like, "I'm going in.
I'm going in."

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.734
-"Felt the vibe."
-And to their credit,

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.000
they were very disarming,
and this and that.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.133
But, yeah, if you --
I think right there,

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:09.167
I'm honestly lost
in Prince William's -- in his --

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.000
in his eyes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.400
-Tell me about this, though.
-His eyes?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.701
-No. But yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.334
-I mean, blue
as the bluest ocean, Jimmy.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.200
What do you want?
-You get right in there,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.033
and you go, "Hi,"
and you just start going gaga?

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.934
-Kind of.
Like, um, and Kate is very --

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:26.834
You know, she's...
-Yeah.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.534
-...beautiful and very,
you know, cordial and...

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:30.968
-Stunning, yeah.
-...holds herself so well.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.634
-Regal.
-Yeah, regal.

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:35.067
And with William, I don't know.
I just --

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.267
[ Laughter ]
I blacked out.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.901
-I just think -- this photo,
I just think --

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.901
And then Jennifer Connelley
looks at you, she goes,

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.534
"That was weird
what you just did to him."

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.167
-'Cause she knew, 'cause I was
standing next to Jen.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.634
So I was kind of --
I don't know.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.767
I was kind of riffing on what --

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.300
what this interaction
was gonna be like.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.467
So I think she was already
on alert about --

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:56.734
if she thought I was gonna
go a bit rogue

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.100
about the whole thing.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.300
But I think he's
a lifelong fan now.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.567
-Yeah, now --
now he has to be, yeah.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:02.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.801
He felt the vibe was the best.
You know --

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.501
-Just picking up
what he was putting down.

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:08.701
-I want to give a shout-out
to your grandma, by the way,

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:09.701
if she's watching.
-Oh, for sure.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.067
-Hi, grandma.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.601
-You're so proud of your
grandson here.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:17.200
She's on Twitter, and she said,
"They're looking for an actor

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.267
to replace Daniel Craig
for a 007.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.167
I think my grandson,
Miles Teller,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.667
has proven that he has
everything they're looking for.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.934
Talent, looks, strength,
worldwide appeal,

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.868
and, oh, so cool."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.834
"He can be that guy!!
Wouldn't he be great?"

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:35.234
♪♪

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.734
-Yeah.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.067
-You had no idea
she was going to do this?

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:41.200
-No.
And I'm not -- look.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.767
I set her up
her Twitter many years ago.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:45.868
-Yeah.
-I'm not gonna tell her

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.567
what to do with it.
-No.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.167
-Do what you want, grandma,
you know?

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.601
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.234
-If you want to --
if you want to --

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.067
-But I am actually here
to make an announcement.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.400
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.667
-Still not 007.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.501
-All right, well, hey.
You know -- it's so --

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.601
-Nobody's -- nobody's called.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:03.133
-No one's called yet.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.067
-We got to get Barbara Broccoli
on the phone here

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.901
and make this official.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:08.567
I mean, I could see you as 007.

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.133
-Yeah, why not?
-I mean --

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.834
-Yeah, you know?
What do you guys think?

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.868
-Why not?

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.634
-Mix it up.
-Mix it up.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.300
Why not do it?
-But I am available.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.167
-This is one of my favorite
times of the year,

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:27.701
because this is
"Saturday Night Live"

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:28.901
season premiere time...
-Oh, my God.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.634
-...and I'm so --
As a comedian, even before

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.400
I was on "Saturday Night Live,"
I get excited in September.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.834
I go, "Oh, this is
'Saturday Night Live.'"

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.434
There's some new cast members.
-I know.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.501
-And it's just fun.
We want it, we need it.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:40.868
-Definitely new cast members
this year, yeah.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.100
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
This is fantastic.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.501
-I know, I know.
-Are you nervous?

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.801
Are you excited?
-I'm very --

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.234
Yeah, I mean,
it's all those things.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.767
Like I --
in my family, growing up,

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.734
"SNL" was, you know,
an institution.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.200
It still is.
-Yeah.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.968
-You know, the years that you
were there and before that --

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:56.734
you know, Cheri Oteri and
Will Farrell and Chris Kattan

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.367
and Ana Gasteyer
and Molly Shannon,

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.767
like, those were --
-Love it.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.701
-It was a real thing.
And, you know, my sisters and I

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.868
