and our close family friends,

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.200
it was our collective dream
to one day, you know,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.901
either be a cast member on "SNL"
or to host,

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.667
so, it's very --

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:13.834
-Did you get any advice
from any other --

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.434
-That's why I'm here.
Give me some advice.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.701
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.133
-Like, what do you --
-Uh, yeah.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.534
Try everything.
-Yeah.

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.234
-Try and believe in the writers.
-Sounds like college.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.267
-Believe -- yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:26.934
Believe in the writers.
Believe in the producers.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.267
They're all
the best of the best.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.667
And they'll all just --
and you do it.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:30.968
Whatever works is gonna work.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.167
Just try everything
and just go all out.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.434
It's just -- honestly.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.167
And they all love you already.

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:38.267
I already heard word back
from down the hall.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:39.734
-Okay, good.
-Yeah, and they said,

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:40.968
"Yeah, he's a good guy."
-Okay, good.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.367
-"We love Miles Teller."
-Good, good.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:44.133
-Yeah.
-Guys, I'm freaking out.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.434
-No, yeah.
It's good.

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:46.634
-No, I'm excited.
-You should.

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:47.767
You should freak out
the whole time.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.501
-You know, you're --
I get -- I just --

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:50.868
I'm excited to see
how it all works.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.234
-It's live TV, man.
-You know what I mean?

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:54.934
-It's fun. No one does live TV
anymore, so it's great.

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:55.968
-Yeah.
-So congratulations.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:57.400
Break a leg.
You're gonna be great.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.400
You're gonna be great.
-Thank you.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.567
-And you got
Kendrick Lamar, too.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:00.868
-Oh, my God.
-So everyone's watching

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.100
this Saturday.
It's gonna be fun.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.300
I want to talk to you
about something.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.734
And this is very interesting
to me.

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.567
You're an investor
in this stuff,

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.100
in this beverage called
"Long Drink."

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.634
-Right.
-I like this stuff,

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:11.067
and I didn't know even that you
were an investor in this stuff.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:14.501
-It's fantastic, yeah.
So this -- I got involved, uh,

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.868
I was just -- I made my way
into a liquor store

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:17.934
couple years ago in New York.

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:19.701
I was doing
some grocery shopping,

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:21.734
some odds and ends and things.
-Yeah.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.534
-And, no,
but I tried this stuff,

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:24.968
and, you know, met the guys.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:28.634
And it's basically like the
national beverage of Finland.

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:30.834
They hosted the Olympics
in 1952.

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:33.601
They had to figure out a way
to kind of, you know,

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:36.501
get mass amounts of alcohol
out to people quickly.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.267
They came up with this stuff.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:40.100
Has anybody here tried it?
Have you guys had it?

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.300
-Yeah.
-A couple people --

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.367
a couple very cool people
have tried it.

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:45.000
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.133
-A couple not-so-cool people
need to try it.

00:06:47.133 --> 00:06:49.534
No, but it's really --
I mean, it tastes --

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:51.534
-I loved it.
-It's gin, so it's not --

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.601
you know, it's not a seltzer.
It tastes like a Fresca.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:56.133
It's really refreshing.
Sugar free.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:58.267
The original.
This is strong.

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:00.667
This is like 8.5 --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:02.601
-Really?
-Like 8.5%.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:03.667
-Yeah.
-And then the cranberry

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:05.000
is really nice, but, um --

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.300
-I went with the original,
'cause my wife is Finnish.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:10.267
So we --
when I go, "Honey, this is

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:12.968
the reason for me to drink this
is because of you."

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.067 --> 00:07:16.000
-Yeah, and we have
to finish all of it.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.133
-Ah! I like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:19.934
The Finnish Long Drink --
is that what they ended up

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:21.801
calling -- that was
the name of the beverage?

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:23.267
-So, if you go to Finland,
they have --

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:26.000
I mean, there's a bunch
of different brands kind of

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.767
doing their version
of the Long Drink.

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:30.534
It's like their national
kind of beverage.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:32.567
So, yeah, ours is, you know --

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:34.667
If you go to longdrink.com,
you can find out

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:36.767
where they're selling it
around you, and then you can --

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:37.834
you can try it out.

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:39.334
-It's really --
Should we try one?

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:40.400
Let's go.
-Yeah, I would love to.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.601
-Which one?
-Oh, I was, like, curious

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:42.934
when we were gonna
get to that part.

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:44.534
-I'm gonna go -- I'm gonna go --
I'll go for the strong.

00:07:44.534 --> 00:07:46.033
-There you go.
-I'll go for the strong.

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:47.634
-I'll go original.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:49.400
♪♪

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.334
Little drinking music?
-Yeah.

00:07:51.334 --> 00:07:53.367
Always with the...
-Cheers to you,

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:55.300
cheers to "Top Gun,"
cheers to "Saturday Night Live."

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.267
-Thank you. Appreciate it.
-Miles Teller.

00:07:57.267 --> 00:07:58.801
Congratulations, buddy.

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:03.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.634
Break a leg.

